[{"text": "I now give the floor to his excellency", "start": 2.639, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "Mudin Salim Ahmed Ibraim, Minister for", "start": 4.72, "duration": 7.4}, {"text": "Foreign Affairs of the Sudan.", "start": 7.919, "duration": 4.201}, {"text": "In the name of Allah the most merciful", "start": 31.92, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "and gracious. Peace and blessings be", "start": 33.44, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "upon our prophet and his family and his", "start": 35.6, "duration": 5.119}, {"text": "companions.", "start": 38.8, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "Your Excellency Mr. Kil Rahman,", "start": 40.719, "duration": 4.481}, {"text": "President of the General Assembly at its", "start": 43.12, "duration": 5.439}, {"text": "81st session.", "start": 45.2, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "Your Excellency Mr. Antonio Gutes,", "start": 48.559, "duration": 4.561}, {"text": "Secretary General of the United Nations.", "start": 50.48, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "Excellencies,", "start": 53.12, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "ladies and gentlemen, esteemed", "start": 55.28, "duration": 4.079}, {"text": "delegations.", "start": 57.52, "duration": 3.839}, {"text": "At the outset, I wish to congratulate", "start": 59.359, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "Mr. Khal Rahman on his election as", "start": 61.359, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "president of the general assembly at its", "start": 64.4, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "81st session.", "start": 66.4, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "I wish him every success in the", "start": 68.96, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "discharge of his duties.", "start": 70.799, "duration": 4.401}, {"text": "I also extend my appreciation and", "start": 73.28, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "gratitude to Miss Anelena Berbach for", "start": 75.2, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "her capable stewardship of the previous", "start": 77.92, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "session.", "start": 79.92, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "I would be remiss not to express our", "start": 81.84, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "appreciation to his excellency, Mr.", "start": 83.68, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "Antonio Guter, Secretary General of the", "start": 85.52, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "United Nations, for his defense of", "start": 87.36, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "legitimate causes and his protection of", "start": 89.84, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "the charter.", "start": 92.0, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "He has exerted considerable efforts to", "start": 93.68, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "advance the reform process and to put", "start": 95.84, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "forward initiatives aimed at making the", "start": 98.079, "duration": 4.321}, {"text": "United Nations more effective,", "start": 100.4, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "influential, and representative.", "start": 102.4, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "I stand today before this distinguished", "start": 106.0, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "assembly under deeply regrettable", "start": 108.32, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "circumstances that Sudan never wished to", "start": 110.96, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "witness within an organization founded", "start": 113.68, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "on the principles of sovereign equality", "start": 116.24, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "among states,", "start": 118.32, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "respect for international law and the", "start": 120.24, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "guarantee of equal participation for all", "start": 123.28, "duration": 5.879}, {"text": "member states.", "start": 125.84, "duration": 3.319}, {"text": "His", "start": 129.52, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "Excellency General Abd Fat Al Borhan,", "start": 132.8, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "chairman of the Transitional Sovereign", "start": 137.76, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "Council of the Republic of Sudan,", "start": 139.2, "duration": 6.399}, {"text": "was to stand before you today to address", "start": 142.16, "duration": 6.159}, {"text": "the General Assembly on behalf of the", "start": 145.599, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "Sudanese people and government. However,", "start": 148.319, "duration": 4.481}, {"text": "the host country prevented this by", "start": 150.56, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "failing to issue the visa required for", "start": 152.8, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "his excellency to participate in this", "start": 155.04, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "highlevel segment of the general", "start": 157.92, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "assembly.", "start": 159.84, "duration": 5.119}, {"text": "More regrettably still, this situation", "start": 162.0, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "persisted despite the efforts undertaken", "start": 164.959, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "by the secretariat", "start": 168.0, "duration": 4.319}, {"text": "and despite the secretary general's", "start": 170.48, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "request to the host country", "start": 172.319, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "to issue the entry visa in accordance", "start": 174.879, "duration": 6.401}, {"text": "with its obligations.", "start": 177.84, "duration": 8.16}, {"text": "under the 1947 headquarters agreement.", "start": 181.28, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "Accordingly,", "start": 186.0, "duration": 4.159}, {"text": "the Republic of Sudan calls upon the", "start": 187.84, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "Secretary General, the General Assembly,", "start": 190.159, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "and the Committee on Relations with the", "start": 193.76, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "host country to take the necessary", "start": 195.36, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "measures to safeguard the sanctity of", "start": 198.239, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "the headquarters agreement.", "start": 200.4, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "Sudan further requests that it this", "start": 203.28, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "incident be formally documented and", "start": 205.84, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "examined by the relevant UN mechanisms", "start": 208.4, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "responsible for the implementation of", "start": 211.519, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "the headquarters agreement.", "start": 213.92, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 216.72, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "the need remains urgent for", "start": 219.04, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "comprehensive, equitable, and", "start": 222.0, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "expeditious reform of the international", "start": 224.4, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "system in light of these changes and", "start": 226.4, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "challenges as well as for political", "start": 228.72, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "administration through dialogue, respect", "start": 231.04, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "for international law and the peaceful", "start": 233.44, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "settlement of disputes.", "start": 236.4, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "There is also need for refraining from", "start": 239.2, "duration": 3.759}, {"text": "the use or threat of use of", "start": 241.36, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "international relations and avoiding the", "start": 242.959, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "imposition of coercive sanctions merely", "start": 245.36, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "on the basis of political disagreements", "start": 248.0, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "or the exploitation of these sanctions", "start": 250.0, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "as instruments to achieve specific", "start": 252.56, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "political or economic objectives. Sudan", "start": 254.72, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "has lived under sanctions imposed", "start": 257.919, "duration": 4.481}, {"text": "pursuant to chapter 7 for more than two", "start": 260.16, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "decades. These sanctions have negatively", "start": 262.4, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "affected its economy, security, and", "start": 265.36, "duration": 5.119}, {"text": "territorial integrity.", "start": 268.0, "duration": 4.639}, {"text": "They have undermined Sudin sovereignty", "start": 270.479, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "and status, exacerbated cycles of", "start": 272.639, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "violence affecting the protection of", "start": 276.0, "duration": 3.919}, {"text": "civilians and vulnerable sectors and", "start": 277.919, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "hindered national reconciliation.", "start": 279.919, "duration": 6.241}, {"text": "the continued disregard for and", "start": 283.759, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "violation of the purposes and principles", "start": 286.16, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "of the UN charter through the use or", "start": 289.12, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "threat of use of force in international", "start": 291.84, "duration": 4.639}, {"text": "relations and through interference in", "start": 294.32, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "the internal affairs of states in", "start": 296.479, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "various forms and through disregard for", "start": 298.56, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "the established principles of", "start": 301.52, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "international law", "start": 302.72, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "threaten confidence in the multiral", "start": 305.44, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "international system and in the charter", "start": 307.6, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "of the United Nations itself.", "start": 309.84, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "Hence the need for United Nations reform", "start": 312.56, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "particularly reform of the security", "start": 315.28, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "council.", "start": 317.52, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "Africa should be represented by two", "start": 320.08, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "permanent seats", "start": 322.24, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "and the working methods of the security", "start": 325.6, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "council should be improved in line with", "start": 327.199, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "current developments and realities.", "start": 329.52, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "The international financial system", "start": 333.039, "duration": 3.841}, {"text": "should be reformed so as to ensure", "start": 334.4, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "equality of opportunity in accessing", "start": 336.88, "duration": 3.759}, {"text": "finance and in implementing the", "start": 338.88, "duration": 3.44}, {"text": "Millennium and Sustainable Development", "start": 340.639, "duration": 4.481}, {"text": "Goals as well as climate action.", "start": 342.32, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "Mr. President, we in Sudan are a", "start": 345.12, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "peaceloving nation, but we also seek a", "start": 347.52, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "just peace.", "start": 350.479, "duration": 5.761}, {"text": "Therefore, from this UN hall, we", "start": 353.28, "duration": 6.8}, {"text": "reaffirm that comprehensive, lasting,", "start": 356.24, "duration": 6.959}, {"text": "and just peace in Sudan", "start": 360.08, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "in a manner that ensures the", "start": 363.199, "duration": 4.321}, {"text": "non-recurrence of conflict", "start": 364.8, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "cannot be achieved without ending", "start": 367.52, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "persistent external interference,", "start": 370.4, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "halting the flow of weapons, ammunition,", "start": 373.039, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "and mercenaries into Sudan, dismantling", "start": 375.199, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "the terrorist militia,", "start": 378.56, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "stopping its attacks against civilians,", "start": 380.88, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "cities, civilian objects,", "start": 383.039, "duration": 4.241}, {"text": "infrastructure, dams, medical centers,", "start": 385.12, "duration": 3.919}, {"text": "and hospitals,", "start": 387.28, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "disarming this militia, and ensuring", "start": 389.039, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "that arms remain exclusively in the", "start": 392.56, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "hands of the state and its established", "start": 394.639, "duration": 4.721}, {"text": "legitimate national institutions. We", "start": 396.8, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "also call for the poor support for the", "start": 399.36, "duration": 3.2}, {"text": "steady progress being made by the", "start": 401.36, "duration": 3.04}, {"text": "Sudanese government in the protection of", "start": 402.56, "duration": 3.199}, {"text": "civilians and the peace buildingilding", "start": 404.4, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "process. Mr. President, peace and", "start": 405.759, "duration": 4.321}, {"text": "stability in Sudan cannot be discussed.", "start": 408.0, "duration": 4.639}, {"text": "While the destructive war waged by", "start": 410.08, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "Dagalo's terrorist militia against the", "start": 412.639, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "Sudanese people continues,", "start": 414.4, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "the international community's silence", "start": 417.199, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "and its failure to take steps to deter", "start": 420.0, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "the atrocities and violations committed", "start": 422.479, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "by the rebel militia in Sudan, despite", "start": 424.24, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "the availability of documented and", "start": 426.639, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "credible evidence and its disregard for", "start": 428.08, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "legitimate calls to designate it as a", "start": 431.68, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "terrorist organization and its failure", "start": 433.36, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "to take decisive measures to stem the", "start": 435.84, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "flow of weapons, material and", "start": 437.84, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "mercenaries supporting the terrorist", "start": 440.24, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "militia across our borders", "start": 442.0, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "are the factors that prolong the war and", "start": 445.12, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "encourage", "start": 448.4, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "the militia's continued aggression.", "start": 449.919, "duration": 5.761}, {"text": "Silence regarding the atrocities", "start": 454.0, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "committed by the terrorist militia in", "start": 455.68, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "Sudan is not only shameful, unethical,", "start": 458.16, "duration": 5.439}, {"text": "and complicit. It is a betrayal of the", "start": 461.039, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "civilian victims of women and girls who", "start": 463.599, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "have demonstrated unprecedented", "start": 466.319, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "resilience in enduring suffering beyond", "start": 468.24, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "description", "start": 472.0, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "and indeed of an entire people.", "start": 474.56, "duration": 7.12}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 478.56, "duration": 4.639}, {"text": ">> the call for a comprehensive", "start": 481.68, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "nationallyowned Sudin Sudin dialogue to", "start": 483.199, "duration": 6.641}, {"text": "achieve peace represents one of the key", "start": 486.4, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "pillars of peace and the optimal path", "start": 489.84, "duration": 5.759}, {"text": "for resolving the current crisis.", "start": 492.4, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "However, a conducive environment must be", "start": 495.599, "duration": 4.481}, {"text": "established to ensure its success and", "start": 497.84, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "the achievement of its intended", "start": 500.08, "duration": 3.119}, {"text": "outcomes. This should be through the", "start": 501.44, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "following", "start": 503.199, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "parallel and measurable measures to", "start": 506.08, "duration": 5.119}, {"text": "protect civilians, reduce polarization,", "start": 508.16, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "deescalate tensions and contain", "start": 511.199, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "political estrangement among civilian", "start": 513.519, "duration": 6.241}, {"text": "political and military forces.", "start": 516.0, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "Constructive confidence building", "start": 519.76, "duration": 3.36}, {"text": "measures to provide the dialogue with", "start": 521.36, "duration": 5.559}, {"text": "credibility and legitimacy.", "start": 523.12, "duration": 3.799}, {"text": "the dialogue being conducted through a", "start": 527.44, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "purely Sudanese will free from external", "start": 529.6, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "interference and free from bargaining,", "start": 532.16, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "intimidation and coercion practiced by", "start": 534.399, "duration": 7.56}, {"text": "some parties at these um at present.", "start": 537.12, "duration": 4.839}, {"text": "the implementation of the provisions of", "start": 542.399, "duration": 3.281}, {"text": "the Jedha declaration regarding the", "start": 543.92, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "Sudin armed forces and the rapid support", "start": 545.68, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "forces, including fundamental", "start": 548.32, "duration": 3.36}, {"text": "obligations under international", "start": 550.24, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "humanitarian law, the facilitation of", "start": 551.68, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "humanitarian action, meeting the needs", "start": 554.88, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "of civilians and affected persons, and", "start": 557.04, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "ensuring the safe and voluntary passage", "start": 559.12, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "of civilians leaving areas of", "start": 561.68, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "hostilities.", "start": 563.36, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 566.0, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "past experiences", "start": 568.88, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "and the wars imposed upon Sudan", "start": 570.88, "duration": 6.399}, {"text": "have taught us that peace", "start": 574.8, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "is not achieved merely through the", "start": 577.279, "duration": 3.761}, {"text": "signing of peace agreements without", "start": 579.12, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "addressing the root causes of the crisis", "start": 581.04, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "and eliminating its underlying drivers", "start": 583.12, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "thereby preventing its recurrence.", "start": 586.48, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "Rather, peace is a process requiring", "start": 589.44, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "patience, determination, and commitment", "start": 592.48, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "to addressing the root causes of", "start": 595.12, "duration": 3.839}, {"text": "conflict, removing sources of", "start": 596.72, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "instability, disarming armed groups,", "start": 598.959, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "restricting arms possession to the", "start": 602.24, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "state, and building peace. The state has", "start": 604.399, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "already begun preparations and creating", "start": 607.12, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "a conducive environment for this", "start": 609.44, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "dialogue aimed at reaching common ground", "start": 611.04, "duration": 6.479}, {"text": "through free discussion", "start": 614.16, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "and placing the country on the path", "start": 617.519, "duration": 3.281}, {"text": "towards the most appropriate and", "start": 619.12, "duration": 3.839}, {"text": "inclusive political transition that", "start": 620.8, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "include that excludes no one except", "start": 622.959, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "outlaws and traitors.", "start": 625.44, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "This transition should ultimately lead", "start": 628.32, "duration": 3.759}, {"text": "to free and fair elections in which all", "start": 629.839, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "Sudin participate under international", "start": 632.079, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "and regional observation, allowing our", "start": 634.48, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "people to determine who governs them at", "start": 636.959, "duration": 3.361}, {"text": "the conclusion of the democratic", "start": 638.959, "duration": 3.841}, {"text": "transition.", "start": 640.32, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "Sudan has joined the borrowers platform", "start": 642.8, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "in recognition of the importance of", "start": 645.36, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "development financing. We are actively", "start": 647.68, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "participating in its foundational work", "start": 650.0, "duration": 3.279}, {"text": "in preparation for its first session", "start": 651.6, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "next October. This is undertaken in", "start": 653.279, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "support of efforts to implement a road", "start": 656.32, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "map for debt relief. Sudan also seeks to", "start": 658.32, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "improve relations with international", "start": 661.12, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "financial institutions,", "start": 662.56, "duration": 4.719}, {"text": "secure the lifting of its temporary", "start": 665.04, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "suspension from the international", "start": 667.279, "duration": 4.161}, {"text": "monetary fund and establish development", "start": 668.88, "duration": 4.639}, {"text": "partnerships that will enable it to", "start": 671.44, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "manage the recovery stage. We wish to", "start": 673.519, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "express our sincere gratitude to the", "start": 676.32, "duration": 3.759}, {"text": "least developed countries group for the", "start": 678.079, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "confidence it has placed in us and for", "start": 680.079, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "electing us as vice chair of the group's", "start": 682.079, "duration": 4.561}, {"text": "international coordinating bureau by", "start": 684.72, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "consensus. We shall work to advance its", "start": 686.64, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "development interests and economic", "start": 689.2, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "recovery and ensure a smooth and secure", "start": 691.04, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "graduation from this category.", "start": 694.16, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "In the same spirit, Sudan has been among", "start": 696.8, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "the first countries to join the global", "start": 699.839, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "alliance for south south and triangular", "start": 703.36, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "cooperation.", "start": 705.839, "duration": 3.841}, {"text": "This reflects our belief in the", "start": 708.24, "duration": 3.36}, {"text": "importance of strengthening solidarity,", "start": 709.68, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "mutual benefit, and horizontal", "start": 711.6, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "partnership as an alternative to", "start": 713.92, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "traditional vertical aid-based", "start": 717.04, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "relations.", "start": 719.04, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "We hope that our membership will help", "start": 720.72, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "leverage the considerable influence of", "start": 723.36, "duration": 5.279}, {"text": "this alliance in preparing the country", "start": 725.2, "duration": 7.639}, {"text": "for the post-war period,", "start": 728.639, "duration": 4.2}, {"text": "including economic recovery and", "start": 733.36, "duration": 3.52}, {"text": "reconstruction.", "start": 734.88, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 736.88, "duration": 4.079}, {"text": "we reaffirm Sudan's openness to any", "start": 739.12, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "sincere and constructive effort aimed at", "start": 740.959, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "ending the war imposed on its people,", "start": 742.88, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "thereby securing peace, preserving the", "start": 745.92, "duration": 3.359}, {"text": "unity, territorial integrity, and", "start": 747.68, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "political independence of the state, and", "start": 749.279, "duration": 4.321}, {"text": "preventing the outbreak of another armed", "start": 751.6, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "rebellion. Nevertheless, at the same", "start": 753.6, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "time, we reiterate our categorical", "start": 756.0, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "rejection of any attempt to impose", "start": 758.399, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "solutions, dictates, or external agendas", "start": 760.32, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "upon our people. The Sudin people alone", "start": 763.04, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "are the makers of that decision and will", "start": 766.48, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "determine their future without influence", "start": 768.8, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "or pressure in accordance with the", "start": 770.56, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "principle of national ownership of", "start": 773.12, "duration": 3.36}, {"text": "peaceuilding affirmed in Security", "start": 774.88, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "Council resolution 2736.", "start": 776.48, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "On this basis, we affirm our readiness", "start": 778.8, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "to cooperate constructively with", "start": 781.76, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "initiatives aimed at addressing the root", "start": 783.279, "duration": 4.321}, {"text": "causes of the crisis, ending the unjust", "start": 785.36, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "aggression against our people,", "start": 787.6, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "preserving national state institutions", "start": 790.32, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "and sovereignty,", "start": 792.16, "duration": 3.52}, {"text": "supporting efforts to achieve peace and", "start": 793.92, "duration": 4.159}, {"text": "development, and overcoming current", "start": 795.68, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "challenges.", "start": 798.079, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "We have supported the efforts of the", "start": 800.639, "duration": 3.44}, {"text": "Secretary General's personal envoy for", "start": 802.399, "duration": 3.521}, {"text": "Sudan and his consultations with", "start": 804.079, "duration": 3.841}, {"text": "neighboring countries and we have", "start": 805.92, "duration": 3.599}, {"text": "responded positively to constructive", "start": 807.92, "duration": 3.52}, {"text": "proposals and initiatives aimed at", "start": 809.519, "duration": 4.401}, {"text": "ending the war of aggression. We have", "start": 811.44, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "also advanced a purely Sudin effort to", "start": 813.92, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "overcome the crisis, restore stability", "start": 816.24, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "and rebuild the country. This was", "start": 818.399, "duration": 4.321}, {"text": "embodied in the road map submitted to", "start": 820.639, "duration": 6.161}, {"text": "the security council in December 2025.", "start": 822.72, "duration": 6.239}, {"text": "In parallel, Sudan continues its", "start": 826.8, "duration": 3.599}, {"text": "positive cooperation with the United", "start": 828.959, "duration": 3.841}, {"text": "Nations, including the office of the", "start": 830.399, "duration": 4.081}, {"text": "special representative of the secretary", "start": 832.8, "duration": 6.599}, {"text": "general on sexual violence in conflict.", "start": 834.48, "duration": 4.919}, {"text": "We continue to cooperate with the office", "start": 840.32, "duration": 3.759}, {"text": "of the coordination of humanitarian", "start": 842.56, "duration": 3.12}, {"text": "affairs and the office of the special", "start": 844.079, "duration": 2.961}, {"text": "representative of the secretary general", "start": 845.68, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "for children and armed conflict as well", "start": 847.04, "duration": 7.159}, {"text": "as human rights mechanisms.", "start": 849.6, "duration": 4.599}, {"text": "They have enjoyed support from the", "start": 854.399, "duration": 2.721}, {"text": "government of Sudan, whether through the", "start": 855.68, "duration": 3.279}, {"text": "country office or the designated human", "start": 857.12, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "rights experts on Sudan. We renew our", "start": 858.959, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "appreciation for and support of the", "start": 861.76, "duration": 3.36}, {"text": "positions of sisterly and friendly", "start": 863.6, "duration": 2.88}, {"text": "countries that support Sudan's", "start": 865.12, "duration": 3.04}, {"text": "sovereignty, unity, and national", "start": 866.48, "duration": 3.28}, {"text": "institutions.", "start": 868.16, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "We call upon the international community", "start": 869.76, "duration": 4.639}, {"text": "to capitalize on global momentum and", "start": 871.76, "duration": 5.199}, {"text": "show solidarity with Darur following the", "start": 874.399, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "Daglo militia's takeover of Al Faser and", "start": 876.959, "duration": 4.161}, {"text": "the compelling evidence and testimony", "start": 879.519, "duration": 3.361}, {"text": "presented by the Sultan of the Masalid", "start": 881.12, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "people to the security council. We call", "start": 882.88, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "upon you to advance legal accountability", "start": 884.8, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "processes for the perpetrators. This is", "start": 887.36, "duration": 3.52}, {"text": "one of the effective avenues for", "start": 889.44, "duration": 3.28}, {"text": "deescalation and for curbing the wave of", "start": 890.88, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "violations committed by the militia with", "start": 892.72, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "considerable support from its regional", "start": 894.72, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "and external sponsors.", "start": 896.32, "duration": 5.199}, {"text": "These continued violations alone", "start": 899.76, "duration": 3.199}, {"text": "undermine the credibility of any", "start": 901.519, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "political partnership in the political", "start": 902.959, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "winged wing of the rapid support forces", "start": 905.279, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "militia during the remainder of the", "start": 908.48, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "transition period given its continued", "start": 910.24, "duration": 6.039}, {"text": "and reprehensible complicity.", "start": 912.24, "duration": 4.039}, {"text": "The Security Council has failed to", "start": 922.32, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "condemn and identify the sponsors,", "start": 924.079, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "thereby contributing to the concealment", "start": 927.12, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "of those atrocities. These sponsors have", "start": 929.279, "duration": 4.721}, {"text": "also continued to recruit foreign", "start": 931.6, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "mercenaries and provided political cover", "start": 934.0, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "for the militia's political wing while", "start": 936.0, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "fabricating accusations against the", "start": 938.16, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "Sudin armed forces supported by", "start": 939.76, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "regionally funded platforms backed by", "start": 942.0, "duration": 4.079}, {"text": "the militia sponsors that disseminate", "start": 944.0, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "disinformation baseless allegations and", "start": 946.079, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "fabricated condemnations aimed at", "start": 948.959, "duration": 4.081}, {"text": "tarnishing the reputation of our", "start": 951.04, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "professional armed forces. Our armed", "start": 953.04, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "forces have fought alongside the allies", "start": 955.6, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "during World War II.", "start": 958.0, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "The response has been efforts to", "start": 961.12, "duration": 6.44}, {"text": "undermine and destroy the armed forces", "start": 963.12, "duration": 4.44}, {"text": "and to impose sanctions on their leaders", "start": 968.16, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "and expand the Darur arms embargo to", "start": 969.92, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "encompass all of Sudan. This paves the", "start": 972.24, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "way for the victory of the militia and", "start": 974.48, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "the foreign mercenaries who constitute", "start": 976.0, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "60% of its members.", "start": 978.24, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "Throughout this war of aggression, the", "start": 981.6, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "Sudin armed forces", "start": 983.12, "duration": 3.44}, {"text": "have adhered to the following", "start": 985.36, "duration": 3.36}, {"text": "principles. the protection of civilians", "start": 986.56, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "in accordance with the approved national", "start": 988.72, "duration": 3.919}, {"text": "plan submitted by Sudan to the security", "start": 990.32, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "council.", "start": 992.639, "duration": 3.2}, {"text": "Distinction at all times between", "start": 994.24, "duration": 3.279}, {"text": "combatants and civilians and between", "start": 995.839, "duration": 5.841}, {"text": "civilian objects and military targets.", "start": 997.519, "duration": 5.841}, {"text": "Taking precautionary measures to avoid", "start": 1001.68, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "and minimize incidental harm. Refraining", "start": 1003.36, "duration": 6.839}, {"text": "from using civilians as human shields.", "start": 1005.6, "duration": 4.599}, {"text": "Refraining from recruiting child", "start": 1010.399, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "soldiers.", "start": 1012.399, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "refraining from enforced disappearances", "start": 1014.399, "duration": 3.921}, {"text": "and the arbitrary detention of civilians", "start": 1016.079, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "and adhering to humanitarian truses.", "start": 1018.32, "duration": 6.239}, {"text": "To end the war, pressure must be exerted", "start": 1022.0, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "on the regional sponsors and certain", "start": 1024.559, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "neighboring states that have not merely", "start": 1026.16, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "facilitated the transfer of weapons,", "start": 1028.559, "duration": 3.601}, {"text": "equipment, and supplies to the militia", "start": 1030.72, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "through their territories, but have also", "start": 1032.16, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "created battlefronts and enabled", "start": 1034.48, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "repeated attacks launched by militias", "start": 1036.72, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "and mercenaries from within their", "start": 1038.88, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "territories in broad daylight and", "start": 1040.48, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "established hospitals along their", "start": 1042.88, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "borders to treat militia casualties.", "start": 1044.48, "duration": 5.199}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 1047.52, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "the cause of Palestine remains the", "start": 1049.679, "duration": 3.681}, {"text": "central issue in the Middle East. The", "start": 1051.36, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "Palestinian people must be empowered to", "start": 1053.36, "duration": 2.72}, {"text": "exercise their right to", "start": 1055.2, "duration": 2.719}, {"text": "self-determination and establish their", "start": 1056.08, "duration": 3.839}, {"text": "independent state with Jerusalem as its", "start": 1057.919, "duration": 4.161}, {"text": "capital and refugees must be allowed to", "start": 1059.919, "duration": 3.441}, {"text": "return in accordance with the", "start": 1062.08, "duration": 3.44}, {"text": "resolutions of international legitimacy.", "start": 1063.36, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "Sudan also stresses the importance of", "start": 1065.52, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "stability in the Red Sea, Bab al-Mandab", "start": 1067.84, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "and the Gulf region. given their impact", "start": 1070.559, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "on the wider region. There is a need to", "start": 1073.36, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "end the current situation in a manner", "start": 1075.919, "duration": 3.201}, {"text": "that spares the peoples of the region", "start": 1077.52, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "the scourge of war and its consequences.", "start": 1079.12, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "We reaffirm our full support for the", "start": 1081.52, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "countries of the region in preserving", "start": 1083.28, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "their sovereignty, security and", "start": 1085.28, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "stability. We underscore the importance", "start": 1086.96, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "of respect for international law and the", "start": 1088.88, "duration": 3.52}, {"text": "charter of the United Nations and the", "start": 1090.64, "duration": 2.96}, {"text": "importance of refraining from", "start": 1092.4, "duration": 2.8}, {"text": "interference in the internal affairs of", "start": 1093.6, "duration": 3.04}, {"text": "states.", "start": 1095.2, "duration": 3.839}, {"text": "Before concluding, allow me to convey to", "start": 1096.64, "duration": 5.919}, {"text": "you the greetings of General Abdat Al", "start": 1099.039, "duration": 6.321}, {"text": "Borhan", "start": 1102.559, "duration": 6.161}, {"text": "who is at this moment", "start": 1105.36, "duration": 7.679}, {"text": "among his people as they chant", "start": 1108.72, "duration": 7.92}, {"text": "in one voice, one army, one people", "start": 1113.039, "duration": 6.561}, {"text": "behind their leader.", "start": 1116.64, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "Peace and the mercy and blessings of God", "start": 1119.6, "duration": 4.92}, {"text": "be upon you all.", "start": 1121.039, "duration": 3.481}, {"text": "I thank the Minister for Foreign Affairs", "start": 1130.48, "duration": 5.64}, {"text": "of the Sudan.", "start": 1132.64, "duration": 3.48}]